<title>Try It: Writing Equations Using Graphs in Situations </title>
<para>Use Desmos or a graphing calculator to create a graph for \( 40x +20y = 180 \).</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<!--Q1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>If \(x\) represents the number of pairs of shoes and \(y\) represents the number of pairs of jeans, what is one
        combination that is a solution?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples: \((2, 5)\), \((1, 7)\), \((3, 3)\), \((4,
      1)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --> 
<!--Q2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does the combination you identified mean on the graph? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. For \((2, 5)\), that means buying 2 pairs of
      shoes and 5 pairs of jeans will cost $180. </para>
    <para>This is how to find a solution and determine its meaning:</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item>Find a point on the graph of the line. </item>
      <item>The point \((2, 5)\) is on the graph. Since 2 is the coordinate of the \(x\)-coordinate, it represents 2 pairs of
        shoes. </item>
      <item>Since 5 is the \(y\)-coordinate, it represents 5 pairs of jeans. </item>
      <item>The line represents all combinations that equal $180. </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
